# A Windows-style share name typed in the location bar: on Linux it becomes the smb://
# address GVfs mounts — this share does not exist on the test machine, so the mount fails
# and the message names the address. On Windows such a name is a native path already: the
# bar answers that it cannot find the share, with the name spelled as typed.
path-edit
type-location \\127.0.0.1\My Share\sub dir
!unix wait-dialog Cannot open “smb://127.0.0.1/My%20Share/sub%20dir”
!unix dialog-button Cannot open : Close
!win wait-dialog Location not found
!win dialog-button Location not found : Close
# A plain path still is one.
path-edit
type-location $T
expect-location $T
